{"Title":"An Act relative to local public housing authorities access to the dental and vision insurance plan managed by the group insurance commission","BillNumber":"S1611","DocketNumber":"SD178","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MDB0","Name":"Michael D. Brady","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MDB0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-09T13:52:53.76"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MDB0","Name":"Michael D. Brady","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MDB0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-09T13:52:53.76"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1611/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Brady, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1611) of Michael D. Brady for legislation relative to local public housing authorities access to the dental and vision insurance plan managed by the group insurance commission.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tNotwithstanding Chapter 32A of the General Laws, the Group Insurance Commission shall provide dental and vision insurance benefits to employees of a housing or redevelopment authority upon a vote by its governing body.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}